<title>HONG KONG: HK Tel shares rise on C&amp;W sale report.</title>
<headline>HK Tel shares rise on C&amp;W sale report.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Hong Kong Telecommunications Ltd made firm gains in early trade on Monday following a newspaper report that Cable and Wireless Plc was set to reduce its stake in its Hong Kong unit.</p>
<p>The stock was up HK$0.30 at HK$13.20.</p>
<p>London's Sunday Telegraph said Cable and Wireless was understood to have negotiated a deal with China, which was likely to result in Hongkong Telecom passing into Chinese hands.</p>
<p>It said Cable and Wireless was set to cut is 58.6 percent stake to below 50 percent in return for better access to the China market.</p>
<p>A Hong Kong Telecom official called the report gossip.</p>
</text>
